<article class="env-corollary" id="02U8">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02U8">Corollary <span data-tag="02U8">4.5.8.19</span>.</a> Let $U: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{B}}$ be an exponentiable morphism of simplicial sets. For every $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$, the projection map $\pi : \operatorname{Fun}( \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}/\operatorname{\mathcal{B}}, \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}) \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{B}}$ is an isofibration of simplicial sets. </p>
</article>
